  "version": 1,
  "note": "Synthetic multimodal pseudo-causal corpus (MM3). Every original is a few generated bytes, not a real screenshot, recording or report. Each case writes one claim through Repository.add after registering the originals as attachments. Placeholders in evidence: {att:K} att:<id>, {id:K} the id, {ID:K} it uppercased, {sha:K} the sha256 hex, {SHA:K} it uppercased, {sha16:K} its first 16 hex, {sha_zw:K} the hex with U+200B inside, {file:K} a copy of the original outside the vault, {file_pct:K} that path percent-encoded, {sha_tab:K}/{sha_comma:K}/{sha_slash:K} the hex split by tabs, commas or a slash, {sha_space:K}/{sha_dash:K}/{sha_endash:K}/{sha_nbsp:K} the hex in groups split by spaces, hyphens, en dashes or NBSPs, {sha_plus:K}/{sha_tilde:K} split by + or ~, {b64_spaced:K} base64 in groups of four separated by spaces, {b64:K}/{b64url:K} the digest in base64/base64url, {rel:K} the copy's path relative to the vault, {blob:K} the blob path. A case with `prior` first writes that memory (before the originals are registered when `before_attachments` is true, to exercise the legacy rule), then applies `update` to it.",
